        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=\n{{\n`You are an experienced Human Resources recruitment analyst specialising in food microbiology, food safety and quality assurance recruitment.\n\nYour task is to evaluate a candidate for the position of Quality Control Analyst and Microbiologist at Beneath the Bite Foods Ltd.\n\nJOB REQUIREMENTS\n\nPosition: Quality Control Analyst and Microbiologist\nDepartment: Quality Assurance and Quality Control.\n\nMANDATORY REQUIREMENTS:\n1. A bachelor's degree in Microbiology, Food Science, Biotechnology or a closely related discipline.\n2. At least two years of relevant professional experience in microbiology, quality control, food production, food processing or a related laboratory environment.\n\nDESIRABLE QUALIFICATIONS:\n- MSc or postgraduate qualification in Microbiology, Food Microbiology, Food Science, Biotechnology or Industrial Microbiology.\n- Practical microbiological testing, microbial enumeration, isolation, identification and pathogen detection.\n- Food manufacturing, food processing or quality control laboratory experience.\n- HACCP, GMP and ISO 22000 knowledge or training.\n- Laboratory equipment handling and analytical skills.\n- Environmental monitoring, contamination control and hygiene assessment.\n- Laboratory documentation, SOPs and reporting.\n- Food preservation, fermentation, spoilage or related research experience.\n- Relevant professional certifications and additional training.\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES:\n- Conduct microbiological analysis of raw materials, intermediate products and finished products.\n- Perform microbial enumeration, isolation, identification and pathogen detection.\n- Monitor production hygiene, sanitation and environmental conditions.\n- Maintain laboratory records and prepare technical reports.\n- Identify contamination risks and recommend corrective and preventive actions.\n- Support HACCP implementation and quality control procedures.\n- Monitor critical control points and report deviations.\n- Handle, store and dispose of samples appropriately.\n- Follow laboratory safety requirements and standard operating procedures.\n- Collaborate with production and quality assurance teams.\n\nSCORING FRAMEWORK (100 POINTS):\n1. Relevant academic qualification: 20 points.\n2. Relevant professional experience: 25 points.\n3. Practical microbiology and laboratory skills: 25 points.\n4. Food safety, HACCP, GMP and ISO knowledge: 15 points.\n5. Additional qualifications, certifications and relevant technical skills: 15 points.\n\nASSESSMENT RULES:\n- The relevant bachelor's degree and minimum two years of relevant experience are mandatory.\n- A postgraduate qualification cannot compensate for failure to meet either mandatory requirement.\n- Do not count unrelated employment as relevant professional experience.\n- Do not assume that a candidate possesses a skill or qualification that is not stated in the CV.\n- Distinguish professional experience from internships, academic projects and training.\n- Where information is unclear, state that it requires human verification.\n- Assess candidates fairly and consistently.\n- Do not use age, gender, ethnicity, religion, disability, marital status or other protected personal characteristics in scoring.\n- AI assessment is advisory. Final recruitment decisions must be made by human HR personnel.\n\nRECOMMENDATION RULES:\n- If either mandatory requirement is not met: NOT QUALIFIED.\n- If both mandatory requirements are met and the score is 70 or above: RECOMMEND FOR INTERVIEW.\n- If both mandatory requirements are met and the score is 55–69: HUMAN REVIEW.\n- If both mandatory requirements are met and the score is below 55: NOT RECOMMENDED.\n\nCANDIDATE CV:\n${$json.cv_text}\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON using this exact structure:\n\n{\n  \"candidate_name\": \"\",\n  \"email\": \"\",\n  \"phone\": \"\",\n  \"highest_qualification\": \"\",\n  \"field_of_study\": \"\",\n  \"bachelors_degree_relevant\": true,\n  \"degree_assessment\": \"\",\n  \"years_of_relevant_experience\": 0,\n  \"experience_requirement_met\": true,\n  \"experience_assessment\": \"\",\n  \"technical_skills\": [],\n  \"relevant_experience\": \"\",\n  \"food_safety_knowledge\": \"\",\n  \"professional_certifications\": [],\n  \"strengths\": [],\n  \"skills_gaps\": [],\n  \"qualification_score\": 0,\n  \"experience_score\": 0,\n  \"technical_skills_score\": 0,\n  \"food_safety_score\": 0,\n  \"additional_qualifications_score\": 0,\n  \"total_match_score\": 0,\n  \"mandatory_requirements_met\": true,\n  \"recommendation\": \"\",\n  \"ai_assessment\": \"\",\n  \"human_review_required\": true\n}\n\nEnsure all scores are numeric, the total is out of 100, and the recommendation follows the mandatory requirements and thresholds. Use null for unknown numeric values rather than inventing figures.`\n}}\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "jsonOutput": true,
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
